  "body": "Unless I'm missing something, there's currently no way to listen to changes to `input.validity`.\r\nThe particular case I am interested in is with `<input type=date>`. In chrome, when a user types in part of the date, changing the state from `mm/dd/yyyy` to `01/dd/yyyy`, `input.validity.valid` will change to from true to false.\r\nThis behavior is possible to track by listening to a number of events, such as `keydown`, `keyup`, `paste`, and `cut`, but having to listen to several events for changes to validity isn't the best and I could have even missed an event in the four that I listed that I don't know about.\r\nIn this case, a web developer suggested that we should fire the `input` event when `input.validity` changes. This behavior would go against the spec since the spec currently says that the `input` event is only fired when `input.value` changes, which does not occur when the visible state changes from `mm/dd/yyyy` to `01/dd/yyyy`.\r\nWould it make sense to change the spec to allow `input` to be fired when `input.validity` changes? Would it make sense to add a new event to fire just for `input.validity` changes?",
